| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                                                                           | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|-----------|-----------|----------------|
| G1     | Complete Resource Transfer Mission | Ensure that the requested resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent in the specified location. | **;** | Perform | – | The mission consists of two main phases (collect → deliver) that must be executed in this order. |
| G2     | Collect Resources           | Execute the collection of all required items from the storages. | **FALLBACK((G2.1 ; G2.2), G2.3)** | Perform | AND | The collection can succeed by performing navigation‑request and wait‑for‑retrieval; if a low‑battery situation is detected (G2.3) a fallback to an alternate robot is required. |
| G2.1   | Navigation & Request Resources | Move to the storage, send the request message and wait until the resources are ready for pickup. | **;** | Perform | AND | Navigation must finish before the request can be sent, therefore sequential execution. |
| G2.1.1 | Navigate to Storage         | Robot moves to the storage location where the resources are located. | – | – | – |
| G2.1.2 | Send Request to Storage    | Robot sends a message specifying the exact resources requested. | – | – | – |
| G2.2   | Wait for Retrieval          | Robot waits until the storage confirms that the resources have been retrieved. | – | Perform | AND | The robot cannot continue until the resources are available. |
| G2.3   | Handle Low Battery in Collection | If battery < 10 % during collection, the robot returns to the charging station and assigns the mission to another robot. | – | Perform | AND | This is a concrete action that must be executed when the low‑battery condition is detected. |
| G3     | Deliver Resources           | Move the collected resources to the specified destination and hand them over to the requesting agent. | **FALLBACK((G3.1 ; G3.2), G3.3)** | Perform | AND | Delivery proceeds by navigation and transfer; if battery < 30 % during delivery (G3.3) a fallback is required. |
| G3.1   | Navigation to Destination    | Robot moves from the storage (or checkpoint) to the destination location. | **;** | Perform | AND | The robot must reach the destination before it can transfer the resources. |
| G3.2   | Transfer Resource            | Robot physically hands the resource over to the requesting agent. | – | Perform | AND | Must be executed after navigation. |
| G3.3   | Handle Low Battery in Delivery | If battery < 30 % during delivery, the robot returns the resource to a checkpoint, assigns the remaining task to another robot, and triggers an alert if it fails to return. | **#** | Perform | AND | The three sub‑tasks can occur in parallel (return, assignment, alert). |
| G3.3.1 | Return to Checkpoint        | Robot returns the resource to a pre‑defined checkpoint for safekeeping. | – | Perform | AND | Needed to preserve the resource when low battery is detected. |
| G3.3.2 | Assign Remaining Task       | The robot informs the central controller of the remaining delivery load so that another robot can take over. | – | Perform | AND | Essential for continuity of the mission. |
| G3.3.3 | Trigger Alert               | If the robot fails to return the resource to the checkpoint, an alert is triggered. | – | Perform | AND | Directly follows from the failure condition. |
| G3.3.4 | Send Report to Sector Manager | A detailed report of the failure and current battery level is sent to the sector manager. | – | Perform | AND | Provides situational awareness to higher‑level decision makers. |

